/* ── What the pipeline noticed ──────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * Positional specifiers (%1$@, %2$@) wherever a sentence carries more than
 * one value: Spanish does not always keep the English order, and an
 * unnumbered second %@ would silently take the first argument.
 *
 * The singular and plural forms are separate entries because they are
 * separate keys in Strings.swift. Spanish distinguishes only one from other,
 * the same two forms English needs, so nothing is lost by writing both out.
 */

